    "result_text": "The build passes. Here's what I did.\n\n## Change\n\nIn `OwnerRegistrationDatePolicy.java`, I extended the business-day rule to skip listed public holidays:\n\n- Added a `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` set with the five 2026 dates.\n- Rewrote `rollToBusinessDay` to roll forward one day at a time until it lands on a business day, delegating the \"is this a valid day?\" check to a new small `isBusinessDay` helper that rejects Saturdays, Sundays, and any listed holiday.\n\nThis also fixes a latent gap the old two-`if` version had: rolling a weekend forward now re-checks the landing date, so a holiday adjacent to (or preceding) a weekend is handled correctly.\n\n## Keeping structural impact low\n\n- **One file touched.**\n- The edited method `rollToBusinessDay` dropped from CC 3 to CC 2 (a single `while`), and its changed lines are few.\n- The holiday-membership logic lives in the new cohesive `isBusinessDay` predicate rather than being grown into the existing method, so no single function or class swells.\n\nThe `coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay` acceptance test and the full suite are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
